  <h1>VIPARSPECTRA P2000 vs Spider Farmer SF-2000</h1>
</article>
<figure class="hero">
  <img src="/images/hero-grow-light-electricity-cost.jpg" alt="A 200 watt LED grow light board hanging over a three by three grow tent full of leafy greens" loading="eager" width="1344" height="768" />
</figure>

<div class="article-body">

<h2 id="answer">The Short Answer</h2>

<p>Both of these draw 200 real watts, so they cost the same to run. The <strong>VIPARSPECTRA P2000</strong> is $131.99 and claims a wider veg footprint. The <strong>Spider Farmer SF-2000</strong> is $145.99, states a straight 3x3, uses Samsung LM301B chips, and carries a 4.7 rating across 4,100 reviews against 4.5 across 2,800.</p>

<p>$14 separates them. That is close enough that the choice should come down to your tent, not the price.</p>

<h2 id="power">What You Pay to Run Either One</h2>

<p>Because the draw is identical, the electricity is identical. At 14 hours a day, 200W works out to 2.8 kWh a day, or about <strong>85.2 kWh a month</strong>. Over a year that is roughly 1022 kWh.</p>

<p>This is worth saying out loud because it removes the easiest way to choose wrong. There is no efficiency win to calculate between these two in running cost. The 200W is the 200W.</p>

